  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The short answer",
      "items": [
        "The proxy rejects credential-less traffic early",
        "Then the guards read the Auth.js session or verify an API key hash to get the actor, role and tenant",
        "RBAC checks the permission"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Not shown here",
      "items": [
        "The datastore lookups behind sign-in and key checks, webhook authentication (see the inbound diagram), the config module that decides demo mode, and the individual permissions in the RBAC matrix",
        "Connected but out of scope: Microsoft Teams, DataStore port, Ticket services, Audit chain, Unified intake, Bucket workflow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What it guarantees",
      "items": [
        "In production an unauthenticated request resolves to an actor with no permissions, and an invalid API key never falls back to a privileged identity: the proxy rejects credential-less /api/v1 traffic first, and context.ts returns the inert anonymous actor otherwise"
      ]
    }
  ]
